.TH "RAPTOR" 1 "2026-10" "RAPTOR Studio" "RAPTOR Studio Manual"
.SH NAME
raptor \- RAPTOR Studio: reliability block diagram simulation. With no command, or just a model file, opens the desktop application.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBraptor\fR [\-h] [\-V] [\-v] [\-q] [\-\-log\-level LEVEL] [\-\-log\-file PATH] [\-\-debug] [\-\-config PATH] [\-\-no\-config] [\-\-color {auto,always,never}] [\-\-dev\-features LIST] COMMAND ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
RAPTOR Studio: reliability block diagram simulation. With no command, or just a model file, opens the desktop application.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Global options
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
show program's version number and exit
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
more detail on stderr (repeat: \-vv)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
errors only
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-level\fR \fILEVEL\fR
debug|info|warning|error (default warning)
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-file\fR \fIPATH\fR
also write the log to PATH
.TP
\fB\-\-debug\fR
debug tracing and a native\-crash backtrace (same as RAPTOR_DEBUG=1)
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fIPATH\fR
settings file (default $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/raptor\-studio/config.toml)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-config\fR
ignore the settings file and RAPTOR_* defaults
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI{auto|always|never}\fR
colour output (honours NO_COLOR)
.TP
\fB\-\-dev\-features\fR \fILIST\fR
enable developer options: comma list, 'all' or 'none' (same as RAPTOR_DEV_FEATURES)
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBgui\fR
open the desktop application (the default)
.TP
\fBrun\fR
simulate a model
.TP
\fBvalidate\fR
check models and report errors and warnings
.TP
\fBschema\fR
print the .rbds JSON Schema
.TP
\fBinfo\fR
describe a model: elements, settings, pools
.TP
\fBget\fR
print model fields
.TP
\fBset\fR
change model fields and save the model
.TP
\fBconvert\fR
convert between .rbd, .rbds and AWB .awb
.TP
\fBadvise\fR
say what looks wrong or unwise in a model
.TP
\fBexplain\fR
run a model and say what causes its downtime
.TP
\fBwhatif\fR
compare one or more changes with the open model
.TP
\fBsensitivity\fR
which inputs the answer is most sensitive to
.TP
\fBrecommend\fR
test a change for each top downtime driver
.TP
\fBoptimise\fR
search spares, maintenance or crew sizes for a target
.TP
\fBfit\fR
fit a life law from experience (no data)
.TP
\fBlibrary\fR
part types and assemblies: list, apply, insert, sync
.TP
\fBedit\fR
duplicate elements or copy a block's data
.TP
\fBgroups\fR
list, edit and tag component groups
.TP
\fBimport\-table\fR
import failure/repair, PM or stock values from a spreadsheet
.TP
\fBsweep\fR
run a parameter sweep
.TP
\fBcompare\fR
run two or more models and compare the results
.TP
\fBdiff\fR
show what is different between two models
.TP
\fBestimate\fR
estimate run time before running
.TP
\fBreport\fR
print a stored run's report
.TP
\fBtables\fR
export input and result tables
.TP
\fBrender\fR
draw the diagram to PNG or SVG
.TP
\fBspf\fR
write the Single Point Failure file
.TP
\fBextract\fR
save one hierarchy as a standalone model
.TP
\fBfev\fR
Failure Effects View: fail things, read the effects
.TP
\fBstep\fR
step through a run, printing what each step changed
.TP
\fBmcp\fR
start the MCP server (stdio or HTTP)
.TP
\fBhelp\fR
help for a command or a topic
.TP
\fBconfig\fR
show or change application settings
.TP
\fBcompletion\fR
print a shell completion script
.TP
\fBdoctor\fR
check the installation
.TP
\fBhistory\fR
list, save, describe or restore versions of a model
.TP
\fBhealth\fR
summarise a model's size, completeness and issues
.TP
\fBdeclassify\fR
write a share\-safe copy with names/notes removed
.TP
\fBregister\-file\-types\fR
open .rbds and .rbd files with RAPTOR Studio (this user only)
.TP
\fBanalytic\fR
exact reliability/availability of a coherent RBD
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Open the desktop application.
.RS
.nf
\fBraptor\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Open pump.rbd in the desktop application.
.RS
.nf
\fBraptor pump.rbd\fR
.fi
.RE
.PP
Simulate 100 runs and read one number.
.RS
.nf
\fBraptor run pump.rbd \-n 100 \-f json | jq .summary.Availability\fR
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBraptor\-gui\fR(1), \fBraptor\-run\fR(1), \fBraptor\-validate\fR(1), \fBraptor\-schema\fR(1), \fBraptor\-info\fR(1), \fBraptor\-get\fR(1), \fBraptor\-set\fR(1), \fBraptor\-convert\fR(1), \fBraptor\-advise\fR(1), \fBraptor\-explain\fR(1), \fBraptor\-whatif\fR(1), \fBraptor\-sensitivity\fR(1), \fBraptor\-recommend\fR(1), \fBraptor\-optimise\fR(1), \fBraptor\-fit\fR(1), \fBraptor\-library\fR(1), \fBraptor\-edit\fR(1), \fBraptor\-groups\fR(1), \fBraptor\-import\-table\fR(1), \fBraptor\-sweep\fR(1), \fBraptor\-compare\fR(1), \fBraptor\-diff\fR(1), \fBraptor\-estimate\fR(1), \fBraptor\-report\fR(1), \fBraptor\-tables\fR(1), \fBraptor\-render\fR(1), \fBraptor\-spf\fR(1), \fBraptor\-extract\fR(1), \fBraptor\-fev\fR(1), \fBraptor\-step\fR(1), \fBraptor\-mcp\fR(1), \fBraptor\-help\fR(1), \fBraptor\-config\fR(1), \fBraptor\-completion\fR(1), \fBraptor\-doctor\fR(1), \fBraptor\-history\fR(1), \fBraptor\-health\fR(1), \fBraptor\-declassify\fR(1), \fBraptor\-register\-file\-types\fR(1), \fBraptor\-analytic\fR(1), \fBraptor\-set\-paths\fR(7), \fBraptor\-config\fR(5)
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
\fB0\fR
success
.TP
\fB1\fR
runtime error
.TP
\fB2\fR
usage error
.TP
\fB3\fR
model invalid (validation errors)
.TP
\fB4\fR
model refused: a shape that cannot be run
.TP
\fB5\fR
timed out or aborted; partial results written
.TP
\fB6\fR
output could not be written
.TP
\fB130\fR
interrupted (Ctrl\-C); partial results written
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBRAPTOR_DEBUG\fR
same as \-\-debug
.TP
\fBRAPTOR_DEV_FEATURES\fR
same as \-\-dev\-features
.TP
\fBRAPTOR_CONFIG\fR
path of the settings file (same as \-\-config)
.TP
\fBRAPTOR_WORKSPACE\fR
default for \-\-workspace
.TP
\fBRAPTOR_SEED\fR
salt for every random stream (same as \-\-seed)
.TP
\fBNO_COLOR\fR
disable colour output
.TP
\fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME, XDG_DATA_HOME\fR
base directories
.SH FILES
.TP
\fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/raptor\-studio/config.toml\fR
settings file (see raptor\-config(5))
.TP
\fB$XDG_DATA_HOME/raptor\-studio/mcp\fR
default MCP server workspace
